# ==========================================================
# dropQbsd -- integrity_setup
#
# Copy-paste commands to configure signify(1) integrity
# verification after an install or an update.
#
# This file is a TEMPLATE, not a script. It is printed by:
#   - installer/lib/integrity   (setup_integrity)
#   - installer/lib/checklist   (print_manual_steps)
#   - admin/sign_filelist       (when the private key is missing)
#
# Installed as /opt/dropQbsd/templates/integrity_setup by
# copy_scripts. The live copy is read with:
#   cat /opt/dropQbsd/templates/integrity_setup
#
# Permissions: 644 root:wheel
#
# Requirements:
#   - signify(1)
#       FreeBSD: pkg install signify
#       OpenBSD: in the base system
#   - sha256(1): in the base system on both platforms
#
# Notes:
#   - Run the commands as root.
#   - The private key is encrypted: a passphrase is asked once,
#     at signing time. Keep the passphrase elsewhere.
#   - Cron never needs the private key; verification is
#     public-key only.
#   - Re-run Sign after any change to a monitored file.
#   - Do not put the private key in the repository or in a
#     world-readable location.
# ==========================================================

# FreeBSD: install signify first. OpenBSD ships signify in the
# base system; skip the pkg install line there.
#
# pkg install signify

cd /opt/dropQbsd
rm -f /root/dropQbsd.sec keys/dropQbsd.pub keys/dropQbsd_scripts.sha256.sig
signify -G -e -p keys/dropQbsd.pub -s /root/dropQbsd.sec
chmod 600 /root/dropQbsd.sec
cp templates/filelist_for_etc /etc/dropQbsd/filelist
chown root:wheel /etc/dropQbsd/filelist
chmod 644 /etc/dropQbsd/filelist
Sign
Verify
